<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιγός</span></b>  (A), ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ruin, havoc</i>, of death by
			plague, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμῖν ἀπὸ λ. ἀμῦναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.67
				</span></i>
			; by war, <i><span class="en">
				5.603
			</span></i>, etc.; of <i>destruction</i> of ships, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεῶν ἀπὸ λ. ἀμύνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					16.80
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. Ἐνυαλίου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					9.37
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοᾷ λοιγὸν Ἐρινύς</span>
			(Schütz <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοιγὸς Ἐρινύν</span>)
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ch.</u>
				402
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνδροκμὴς λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					679
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).—Poet. (not in <i><span class="en">
				Od.
			</span></i>); mock-heroic in <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.
				171
			</span></i>. (Cf. Lith. <i>pa-liegti</i> 'become feeble,
		sickly'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
